docs {
  # Admin → Settings (project sections)
  
  Session-auth Inertia routes under `/settings/*` (externa-core **1.3.0** / #201).
  
  Permission: `CanManageProjectSettings`. Not Public API Bearer auth.
  
  ## Auth in Bruno
  
  Same as other `Admin/` requests:
  
  1. Sign in at `{{base_url}}` in a browser
  2. Copy the session cookie into a `Cookie:` header
  3. For mutating requests (`PUT` / `POST`), also send CSRF (`X-XSRF-TOKEN` from the `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie, URL-decoded) — Laravel rejects bare POSTs without it
  
  Expected statuses without a valid session/CSRF: **302** login redirect, **419** CSRF, or **403**.
  
  ## Section route map (#201)
  
  | Section | GET (edit) | PUT (update) |
  |---------| | ---------- | ------------ |
  | General (name, description, url, report_*) | `/settings/project` | same |
  | Localization | `/settings/project/localization` | same |
  | Authentication & Security (+ OIDC, registration) | `/settings/project/security` | same |
  | Content (revisions, preview URL) | `/settings/project/content` | same |
  | Files & Media | `/settings/project/files` | same |
  | API (CORS origins) | `/settings/project/api` | same |
  | Integrations (webhooks + Slack/Telegram) | `/settings/project/integrations` | same |
  | Appearance → Sidebar modules | `/settings/appearance/sidebar` | same |
  
  Each `PUT` saves **only that section’s keys**. Empty write-only secrets (`webhook_secret`, `oidc_client_secret`, `notifier_telegram_bot_token`) keep the stored value.
  
  ## Test / ping endpoints
  
  | Action | Preferred (1.3.0) | Deprecated alias (kept one minor) |
  | ------ | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |
  | Webhook `ping` | `POST /settings/project/integrations/webhook-test` | `POST /settings/project/webhook-test` |
  | Slack notifier test | `POST …/integrations/slack-notifier-test` | `POST /settings/project/slack-notifier-test` |
  | Telegram notifier test | `POST …/integrations/telegram-notifier-test` | `POST /settings/project/telegram-notifier-test` |
  
  Webhook URL + secret must be configured under **Integrations** before the ping succeeds.
  
  ## Related Public API notes
  
  - CORS origins edited here gate Public API when non-empty (see `PublicApi/` folder docs).
  - API **keys** (scopes / rate limits) stay under Access → API Keys, not these routes.
}
